    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Arrays and matrix functions\n",
        "Some useful array functions are listed below:\n",
        "\n",
        "* `x.view()`: Produces a representation of an array and matrix as another type without copying the data.\n",
        "* `np.asarray()`: Works similarly to `np.asmatrix`, converting input to an array.\n",
        "* `np.shape(x)`, `x.shape`: Returns the size of each dimension.\n",
        "* `np.reshape(x)`, `x.reshape()`: Gives a new shape to an array without changing its data.\n",
        "* `np.size()`, `x.size`: Returns the total number of elements in the array or matrix.\n",
        "* `np.ndim()`, `x.ndim`: Returns the number of dimensions of the array or matrix.\n",
        "* `np.tile()`: Replicates an array according to a specified size vector.\n",
        "* `np.ravel(x)`, `x.ravel()`: Returns a flattened view (1-dimensional) of the array or matrix.\n",
        "* `x.flatten`: Works like `ravel` except that it copies the array when producing the flattened version.\n",
        "*  `x.flat`: Poduces a `np.flatiter` object (flat iterator) which is an iterator over a flattened view of an array.\n",
        "* `np.vstack()`, `np.hstack()`: Stack arrays vertically or horizontally, respectively.\n",
        "* `np.concatenate()`: Concatenates arrays along a specified axis.\n",
        "* `np.split()`, `np.vsplit()`, `np.hsplit()`: Split arrays vertically or horizontally.\n",
        "* `np.delete()`: Returns a new array with sub-arrays deleted along a specified axis.\n",
        "* `np.diag(x)`: Returns the diagonal elements of a squared array as a column vector.\n",
        "* `np.triu()`, `np.tril()`: Return the upper or lower triangular part of an array, respectively.\n",
        "\n",
        "Some illustrative examples are given below. "
      ],
      "id": "9c6fc90a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = np.arange(5)\n",
        "x\n",
        "type(x)"
      ],
      "id": "0944cfba",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Convert x to a matrix\n",
        "y = x.view(type=np.matrix)\n",
        "y\n",
        "type(y)"
      ],
      "id": "2aaf1562",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Convert y back to an ndarray\n",
        "z = y.view(type=np.ndarray)\n",
        "z\n",
        "type(z)"
      ],
      "id": "f3e80cf2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "d7e9a787",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Convert x to a 4x1 array\n",
        "y = np.reshape(x, (4, 1))\n",
        "y"
      ],
      "id": "fb944206",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Convert y to a 1x4 array\n",
        "z = np.reshape(y, (1, 4))  # return 1 by 4 array\n",
        "z"
      ],
      "id": "6600decd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Convert z to a 2x2 array\n",
        "w = np.reshape(z, (2, 2))\n",
        "w"
      ],
      "id": "17904cfb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Total number of elements\n",
        "x = np.random.randn(4, 3)\n",
        "np.size(x)  # as a function\n",
        "x.size  # as an attribute"
      ],
      "id": "30a2d6d3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Number of dimensions\n",
        "x = np.random.randn(4, 3)\n",
        "np.ndim(x)  # as a function\n",
        "x.ndim  # as an attribute"
      ],
      "id": "89f2b671",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Horizontal stacking\n",
        "x = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])\n",
        "x\n",
        "# Stacks x 3-times horizontally\n",
        "z = np.hstack((x, x, x))\n",
        "z"
      ],
      "id": "939cd661",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Vertical stacking\n",
        "y = np.vstack((z, z))  # stacks z 2-times vertically\n",
        "y"
      ],
      "id": "e4d81ba2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Vertical splitting\n",
        "x = np.reshape(np.arange(20), (4, 5))\n",
        "x\n",
        "y = np.vsplit(x, 2)  # vertically split at row 2\n",
        "y"
      ],
      "id": "39c092b5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Delete rows and columns\n",
        "x = np.reshape(np.arange(20), (4, 5))\n",
        "x\n",
        "np.delete(x, 1, 0)  # delete the second row"
      ],
      "id": "1f2c98ab",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.delete(x, [2, 3], 1)  # delete the second and third columns"
      ],
      "id": "620e60ce",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# If axis is None, the object is applied to the flattened array.\n",
        "np.delete(x, [2, 3])  # flat x and then remove second and third elements"
      ],
      "id": "8628e3c7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Diagonal elements\n",
        "x = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])\n",
        "y = np.diag(x)  # return diagonal elements\n",
        "y"
      ],
      "id": "c0b1e5c3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Upper and lower triangular parts\n",
        "x = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])\n",
        "np.tril(x)  # lower triangular part"
      ],
      "id": "cbfceffe",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Rounding functions\n",
        "NumPy offers several functions for rounding:\n",
        "\n",
        "* `np.around`: Rounds to the nearest integer (or to a specified number of decimals).\n",
        "* `np.floor`: Rounds down to the nearest integer (i.e., the largest integer less than or equal to the input).\n",
        "* `np.ceil`: Rounds up to the nearest integer (i.e., the smallest integer greater than or equal to the input)."
      ],
      "id": "f785ce5e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Generate a 2x3 array of draws from N(0,1)\n",
        "x = np.random.randn(2, 3)\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "86c606c4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Round to the nearest integer\n",
        "np.around(x)"
      ],
      "id": "f3a5d450",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Round x to 2 decimals\n",
        "np.around(x, 2)"
      ],
      "id": "d1392305",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x.round(2)  # using the round method"
      ],
      "id": "6cbdaa4d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Round down to the nearest integer\n",
        "np.floor(x)"
      ],
      "id": "bd146cb7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Round up to the nearest integer\n",
        "np.ceil(x)"
      ],
      "id": "58b13f0c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Sorting and Nan functions\n",
        "We list some useful NumPy functions related to sorting and handling `NaN` values below:\n",
        "\n",
        "* `np.sort()`: Sorts the elements of an array.\n",
        "* `x.sort()`: Performs an in-place sort of the array `x`.\n",
        "* `np.argsort()`:  Returns the indices that would sort the array.\n",
        "* `x.max()`/ `x.min()`: Return the maximum or minimum value in the array `x`.\n",
        "* `np.amax()` / `np.amin()`:  Return the maximum or minimum value in the array.\n",
        "* `np.argmax()` / `np.argmin()`:  Return the index of the maximum or minimum element.\n",
        "* `np.maximum()` / `np.minimum()`:  Return the maximum/minimum of two arrays.\n",
        "* `np.nan`: Represents \"Not a Number\" (`NaN`), used for missing or undefined values.\n",
        "* `np.inf`: Represents positive infinity.\n",
        "* `np.nansum()`: Returns the sum of array elements, ignoring NaNs.\n",
        "* `np.nanmax()`, `np.nanmin()`: Return the maximum or minimum, ignoring NaNs.\n",
        "* `np.nanargmax()`, `np.nanargmin()`: Return the index of the maximum or minimum, ignoring NaNs.\n",
        "\n",
        "Some illustrative examples are given below."
      ],
      "id": "7e6cee4d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Generate a 4x2 array of draws from N(0,1)\n",
        "x = np.random.randn(4, 2)\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "b7f2880e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.sort(x)  # sort across columns"
      ],
      "id": "49d4c4b5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.sort(x, 0)  # sort across rows"
      ],
      "id": "6ae0d1d0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Generate 3 draws from N(0,1)\n",
        "x = np.random.randn(3)\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "6c88083b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.sort(x)  # does not change x\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "27e835ea",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = np.random.randn(3, 4)\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "f8cc8161",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.amax(x)  # maximum element\n",
        "x.max()  # maximum element\n",
        "x.max(0)  # maximum element across rows\n",
        "x.max(1)  # maximum element across columns"
      ],
      "id": "e85e941e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = np.random.randn(4)  # generate 4 draws from N(0,1)\n",
        "y = np.random.randn(4)  # generate 4 draws from N(0,1)\n",
        "np.maximum(x, y)"
      ],
      "id": "482ae617",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x = np.random.randn(5)  # generate 4 draws from N(0,1)\n",
        "x[1] = np.nan\n",
        "x[3] = None\n",
        "x"
      ],
      "id": "24e86560",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.max(x)  # return nan\n",
        "np.nanmax(x)  # ignore nan value\n",
        "np.sum(x)  # return nan\n",
        "np.nansum(x)  # ignore nan value"
      ],
      "id": "8647455a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Linear algebra functions\n",
        "The linear algebra functions are provided in the `linalg` module. For more information, see the [Linear algebra](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/routines.linalg.html) section from the NumPy documentation. Below, we list some useful linear algebra functions for econometric analysis. \n",
        "\n",
        "* `np.linalg.matrix_power(A, n)`: Raises the square matrix A to the integer power n.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.svd(A)`: Computes the singular value decomposition of matrix A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.cond(A)`: Computes the condition number of matrix A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.slogdet()`: Computes the sign and logarithm of the absolute value of the determinant of a square matrix A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.solve(X, y)`: Solves $X\\beta=y$ for $\\beta$ when $X$ is invertible.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.lstsq(X, y)`: Returns the least squared solution of $y=X\\beta$.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.cholesky(A)`: Returns the Cholesky decomposition of A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.det(A)`: Returns the determinant of A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.eig(A)`: Computes the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.inv(A)`: Computes the inverse of A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.kron(x,y)`: Computes the kronecker product $x\\otimes y$.\n",
        "* `np.trace(A)`: Computes the trace of A.\n",
        "* `np.linalg.matrix_rank(A)`: Computes the rank of A using the SVD method.\n",
        "\n",
        "Some illustrative examples are given below."
      ],
      "id": "afed2534"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Solve the equation Xb=y for b\n",
        "X = np.array([[1.0, 2.0, 3.0], [3.0, 3.0, 4.0], [1.0, 1.0, 4.0]])\n",
        "y = np.array([[1.0], [2.0], [3.0]])\n",
        "np.linalg.solve(X, y)"
      ],
      "id": "c7a45d65",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Inverse of X\n",
        "X = np.matrix([[1, 0.5], [0.5, 1]])\n",
        "np.linalg.inv(X)"
      ],
      "id": "edd9549b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Determinant of X\n",
        "np.linalg.det(X)"
      ],
      "id": "9c2789b4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Eigenvalues and eigenvectors of M\n",
        "M = np.matrix([[1, 0.5], [0.5, 1]])\n",
        "val, vec = np.linalg.eig(M)\n",
        "# Verify the spectral decomposition\n",
        "vec * np.diag(val) * vec.T"
      ],
      "id": "57c82a6a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Rank of X\n",
        "X = np.array([[1, 0.5], [1, 0.5]])\n",
        "np.linalg.matrix_rank(X)"
      ],
      "id": "08d5c35a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
  ],
